   "branch": "judicial",
   "description": "Created by the Twenty-Seventh Amendment (2025); hears major constitutional matters formerly heard by the Supreme Court. Constitutional size is one chief justice plus judges set by Parliament or, pending legislation, the President. Thirteen authorized positions, seven reported filled on the cutoff. The inaugural chief and initial judges were exceptionally appointed by the President on prime-ministerial advice; later appointments follow the Judicial Commission procedure, not popular judicial elections.",
